§§ `Validation Functions`

GIVEN code IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %code% has two characters and no lower-case letters, like an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code
`is valid ISO 3166-1 alpha-2` MEANS
    STRINGLENGTH code EQUALS 2
    AND code EQUALS TOUPPER code

GIVEN code IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %code% has three characters and no lower-case letters, like an ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 code
`is valid ISO 3166-1 alpha-3` MEANS
    STRINGLENGTH code EQUALS 3
    AND code EQUALS TOUPPER code

GIVEN code IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %code% has two non-lower-case characters, a hyphen and at least one more character, like an ISO 3166-2 code
`is valid ISO 3166-2` MEANS
    STRINGLENGTH code AT LEAST 4
    AND SUBSTRING code 0 2 EQUALS TOUPPER (SUBSTRING code 0 2)
    AND SUBSTRING code 2 1 EQUALS "-"


§§ `Country Name Lookup`

GIVEN code IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING STRING
@nlg the country name for alpha-2 code %code%
`country name from alpha-2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF code EQUALS `United States alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "United States"
        IF code EQUALS `United Kingdom alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "United Kingdom"
        IF code EQUALS `Canada alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Canada"
        IF code EQUALS `Australia alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Australia"
        IF code EQUALS `Germany alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Germany"
        IF code EQUALS `France alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "France"
        IF code EQUALS `China alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "China"
        IF code EQUALS `Japan alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Japan"
        IF code EQUALS `Singapore alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Singapore"
        IF code EQUALS `India alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "India"
        IF code EQUALS `Brazil alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Brazil"
        IF code EQUALS `Mexico alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Mexico"
        IF code EQUALS `Switzerland alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Switzerland"
        IF code EQUALS `Netherlands alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Netherlands"
        IF code EQUALS `Sweden alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Sweden"
        IF code EQUALS `New Zealand alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "New Zealand"
        IF code EQUALS `South Korea alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "South Korea"
        IF code EQUALS `Italy alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Italy"
        IF code EQUALS `Spain alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Spain"
        IF code EQUALS `Hong Kong alpha-2` THEN RIGHT "Hong Kong"
        OTHERWISE LEFT (CONCAT "Unknown country code: ", code)

GIVEN code IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING STRING
@nlg the country name for alpha-3 code %code%
`country name from alpha-3` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF code EQUALS `United States alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "United States"
        IF code EQUALS `United Kingdom alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "United Kingdom"
        IF code EQUALS `Canada alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Canada"
        IF code EQUALS `Australia alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Australia"
        IF code EQUALS `Germany alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Germany"
        IF code EQUALS `France alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "France"
        IF code EQUALS `China alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "China"
        IF code EQUALS `Japan alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Japan"
        IF code EQUALS `Singapore alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Singapore"
        IF code EQUALS `India alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "India"
        IF code EQUALS `Brazil alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Brazil"
        IF code EQUALS `Mexico alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Mexico"
        IF code EQUALS `Switzerland alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Switzerland"
        IF code EQUALS `Netherlands alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Netherlands"
        IF code EQUALS `Sweden alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Sweden"
        IF code EQUALS `New Zealand alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "New Zealand"
        IF code EQUALS `South Korea alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "South Korea"
        IF code EQUALS `Italy alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Italy"
        IF code EQUALS `Spain alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Spain"
        IF code EQUALS `Hong Kong alpha-3` THEN RIGHT "Hong Kong"
        OTHERWISE LEFT (CONCAT "Unknown country code: ", code)


§§ `Code Conversion Functions`

GIVEN alpha2 IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING STRING
@nlg the alpha-3 code matching alpha-2 code %alpha2%
`alpha-2 to alpha-3` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `United States alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `United States alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `United Kingdom alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `United Kingdom alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Canada alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Canada alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Australia alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Australia alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Germany alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Germany alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `France alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `France alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `China alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `China alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Japan alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Japan alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Singapore alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Singapore alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `India alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `India alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Brazil alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Brazil alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Mexico alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Mexico alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Switzerland alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Switzerland alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Netherlands alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Netherlands alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Sweden alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Sweden alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `New Zealand alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `New Zealand alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `South Korea alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `South Korea alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Italy alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Italy alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Spain alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Spain alpha-3`
        IF alpha2 EQUALS `Hong Kong alpha-2` THEN RIGHT `Hong Kong alpha-3`
        OTHERWISE LEFT (CONCAT "Cannot convert unknown alpha-2 code: ", alpha2)

GIVEN alpha3 IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING STRING
@nlg the alpha-2 code matching alpha-3 code %alpha3%
`alpha-3 to alpha-2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `United States alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `United States alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `United Kingdom alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `United Kingdom alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Canada alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Canada alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Australia alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Australia alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Germany alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Germany alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `France alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `France alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `China alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `China alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Japan alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Japan alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Singapore alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Singapore alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `India alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `India alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Brazil alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Brazil alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Mexico alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Mexico alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Switzerland alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Switzerland alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Netherlands alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Netherlands alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Sweden alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Sweden alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `New Zealand alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `New Zealand alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `South Korea alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `South Korea alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Italy alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Italy alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Spain alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Spain alpha-2`
        IF alpha3 EQUALS `Hong Kong alpha-3` THEN RIGHT `Hong Kong alpha-2`
        OTHERWISE LEFT (CONCAT "Cannot convert unknown alpha-3 code: ", alpha3)
